\paragraph{Uncertainty estimation and MBR.}
Our selection instantiates MBR decoding \cite{eikema2022sampling, denero2009fast}; despite MBR's success in translation \cite{freitag2022high} and code generation \cite{jinnai2024mbr}, all variants fail to improve over greedy due to instance degeneracy (Appendix~\ref{app:mbr_connection}).
\citet{eikema2025structured} find MBR utilities degrade on structured outputs; our four-stage cascade localizes this failure (\S\ref{sec:selection_gap}).

\paragraph{Capability ceiling vs.\ diversity collapse.}\label{sec:yun_contrast}
\citet{yun2025price} identify \textit{diversity collapse} under constrained decoding; our LP compression corroborates this but differs in scope (agreement-quality correlation vs.\ generation diversity), diagnostic depth, and prescriptive outcome (\S\ref{sec:prescriptive}; Table~\ref{tab:differentiation}).

tool_args.new_string:
\noindent\textbf{Remark.}
Set-level F1 admits no closed-form threshold \cite{dembczynski2011exact}; we use $\alpha{=}1$ throughout, which induces similar thresholds for typical NER sizes ($|E_\cup| \leq 30$).
Signal weights $w_i$ yield quality-weighted MBR: $\hat{p}_w(e) = \sum_{i} w_i \, \mathbf{1}[e {\in} y_i] / \sum_{i} w_i$; weighting improves when $w_i$ correlates with instance quality but degrades otherwise (\S\ref{sec:selection_method}).

