\subsection{Prescriptive Results}\label{sec:prescriptive}

\paragraph{Entity-level construction (exploratory).}
We aggregate entities across samples, retaining those exceeding $\theta{=}2/N$, with LP-weighted or uniform scoring ($\theta$ stable in $[0.15, 0.35]$; Appendix~\ref{app:theta_sweep}).
LP-weighted construction yields $+1.40{\pm}0.51$\,pp on Few-NERD ($p{<}0.001$; Holm $p_{\text{adj}}{=}0.006$, $k{=}10$; Table~\ref{tab:entity_construction}), a smaller non-significant $+0.32$\,pp on SciERC, and no gain on CoNLL ($-0.39$\,pp).\footnote{Holm--Bonferroni \cite{holm1979simple} within families ($k{=}10$, $21$, $9$); global $k{=}57$: $p_{\text{adj}}{=}0.055$ (Appendix~\ref{app:holm}).}
Gains require both low degeneracy \textit{and} LP-F1 alignment (Few-NERD: $D{=}13$\%, headroom${=}12.4$\,pp); $k$ values are validated per family ($k{=}10$, $21$, $9$).
Construction and LP selection are complementary ($\rho_{\text{adj}}$: Few-NERD $0.516$, SciERC $0.167$); QE signals support selective prediction ($+5$--$8$\,pp F1 at 80\% coverage; Table~\ref{tab:cross_selection}).
